From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:59:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] A small prop in a building's sun shadow marked so by the
 game; its own outline no longer taken for one it stands in (SDK_PORT_3DS)

A small prop whose sun shadow is its outline (a bench, a sign, the
Hallowed Tower) has 0x10000000 (NITRO_GX3D_TAG_PROP_SHADED) in its mark
while its place is inside a building's outline of the frame before
(MapProp_PortInShade, as a building's own shade is told): the port draws
it in that shade. The port no longer looks on the screen for the outlines
such a prop's feet are in: its own outline was one of them whenever its
batches didn't come just before the prop's in the scene, and the Hallowed
Tower on Route 209 was drawn as dark as in a building's shade (on a 3DS,
2026-11-12: "Spiritomb's tomb is being incorrectly darkened").
---
 src/overlay005/map_prop.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/overlay005/map_prop.c b/src/overlay005/map_prop.c
index 8b27bc6c..0af87fbb 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/map_prop.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/map_prop.c
@@ -897,6 +897,15 @@ static void MapProp_PortBegin(const MapProp *prop, int index, const AreaDataMana
         // sliver, 2026-11-12, "Bench shadows are not working".
         if (MapProp_PortBuildingShadow(prop, position, rotation, scale, TRUE)) {
             mark |= 0x20000000;
+
+            // (standing in a building's shadow: 0x10000000,
+            // NITRO_GX3D_TAG_PROP_SHADED, and the port draws it in that
+            // shade. The port no longer looks for the outlines its feet are
+            // in on the screen: its own was one of them, and the Hallowed
+            // Tower was as dark as in a building's shade, 2026-11-12)
+            if (MapProp_PortInShade(position)) {
+                mark |= 0x10000000;
+            }
         }
     }
 
